  "task": {
    "objective": "Retrieve the three finite coded caches under real illumination and carry them to the central socket, while retaining safe shadow crossings and enough shared lamp charge. Cache owners have different delivery deadlines.",
    "natural_termination": "All three caches delivered, or all roles have three exposures. Otherwise truncate after 128 live transitions. Stunned or disabled roles may only wait, but the episode can continue for partners.",
    "interaction": "Rotating or switching a shared lamp changes other roles illumination, native visibility, safe crossing and cache access. Shutters occlude real ray segments and walking, portable mirrors turn rays, and finite packs/socket stock fund future partner opportunities. Captures can repeat unless partners darken the occupied watched cell.",
    "observation_access": "Partial native observation. Geometry, wired devices, complete beam/shadow raster, socket stock, deadlines and alarm flags are public. Agents are visible within Manhattan distance two or when their cell is lit, plus self. Mirrors are visible by the same distance/light rule or to their carrier. Cache positions, code, status and carrier are visible within distance two, when lit, or to their same-index owner through its tracker. Unseen record fields are -1 and each record has its explicit role-specific visibility bit. No other-role mask rows enter that role observation."
  },
